WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.084 --> 00:00:02.794
From crushing wrestlers
in the ring

00:00:02.878 --> 00:00:05.130
to crushing
box office records,

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:07.257
Dwayne Johnson
has spent the last 20 years

00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:09.843
becoming
a blockbuster behemoth.

00:00:10.427 --> 00:00:13.889
He now stars alongside
Ryan Reynolds and Gal Gadot

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.058
in Red Notice on Netflix.

00:00:16.141 --> 00:00:17.226
This is my best friend.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:21.939
-We're not friends.
-We're best friends.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.899
But how did he get here?

00:00:23.982 --> 00:00:25.901
Strap in,
put the pedal to the metal,

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:28.904
and prepare to speed
down his road to Netflix.

00:00:31.532 --> 00:00:34.284
Dwayne Johnson's career
kicked off in 1996

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.411
under a less familiar name.

00:00:36.495 --> 00:00:38.830
He stepped into
the WWF wrestling ring

00:00:38.914 --> 00:00:40.123
as Rocky Maivia.

00:00:40.958 --> 00:00:42.376
He was sweet and earnest,

00:00:42.459 --> 00:00:45.838
but it was his reinvention
as wrestling heel "The Rock"

00:00:45.921 --> 00:00:47.256
that would see him
become the face

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:48.841
of late-90s wrestling

00:00:48.924 --> 00:00:51.885
and the master
of the catchphrase.

00:00:51.969 --> 00:00:58.308
If you smell
what The Rock is cookin'!

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:01.812
Skip to 2019
and he'd play himself

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.564
in Fighting with My Family,

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:04.898
where he meets
Florence Pugh's

00:01:04.982 --> 00:01:06.567
wannabe brawler Paige

00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:09.528
and explains the secret
to his in-ring persona.

00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:12.322
The Rock is me,
Dwayne Johnson,

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:13.657
just with the volume
turned way up,

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.076
the treble adjusted,
the base, same guy.

00:01:17.119 --> 00:01:19.705
Wrestling popularity led
to his first acting work

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:20.706
in 1999,

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.375
where he appeared
in That '70s Show

00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:24.918
playing his own father,

00:01:25.002 --> 00:01:27.629
another famed wrestler,
Rocky Johnson.

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.548
You know, I got a son,

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:30.465
and one day,

00:01:30.549 --> 00:01:33.468
he's going to become
the most electrifying man

00:01:33.552 --> 00:01:35.220
in sports entertainment.

00:01:37.556 --> 00:01:40.559
And in 2000, his wrestling
career went intergalactic

00:01:40.642 --> 00:01:42.477
when he starred
in an episode

00:01:42.561 --> 00:01:44.229
of Star Trek: Voyager.

00:01:44.313 --> 00:01:46.190
Resistance is futile.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:47.399
So is all your talk.

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.991
Dwayne's film career
kicked off in 2001,

00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:58.076
where he sold his soul
for eternal life

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.038
as the Scorpion King
in The Mummy Returns.

00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.916
You can put his head
on a CG scorpion's body,

00:02:03.999 --> 00:02:06.460
but there's no
mistaking that attitude.

00:02:07.836 --> 00:02:09.254
He impressed
producers so much

00:02:09.338 --> 00:02:11.632
that an entire prequel
was built for the character,

00:02:11.715 --> 00:02:13.258
giving Dwayne
his first leading role

00:02:13.342 --> 00:02:15.928
in 2002's The Scorpion King,

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:19.181
a great showcase
for his physical abilities

00:02:19.264 --> 00:02:21.934
and that world-famous
eyebrow.

00:02:22.017 --> 00:02:23.769
And it gets so lonely.

00:02:29.066 --> 00:02:31.151
In 2003,
he headed to the jungle

00:02:31.235 --> 00:02:33.862
as bounty hunter Beck
in The Rundown.

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:36.532
Cementing him as the action
star of the moment,

00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:38.492
he even got
an in-film endorsement

00:02:38.575 --> 00:02:40.869
from another
action film legend.

00:02:42.913 --> 00:02:43.914
Have fun.

00:02:46.291 --> 00:02:48.460
Based on 2004's
Walking Tall,

00:02:48.544 --> 00:02:50.796
Arnie passed the torch
to the right guy,

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:53.423
as Dwayne took down
a crooked casino,

00:02:53.507 --> 00:02:56.134
armed only with a big stick.

00:02:58.929 --> 00:03:02.808
Then, he was off to Mars
as Sarge in 2005's Doom,

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:05.060
an adaptation
of the popular video game

00:03:05.143 --> 00:03:07.646
and a rare villainous role
for our star.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:09.773
Good luck with that,
Karl Urban.

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:12.401
2005 also let Dwayne

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:15.821
flex his dramatic muscles
in Be Cool.

00:03:15.904 --> 00:03:19.074
He also got to show off
some very groovy trousers.

00:03:21.577 --> 00:03:22.411
Scorchin'!

00:03:22.494 --> 00:03:25.622
And 2006 saw him stepping
into the dystopian world

00:03:25.706 --> 00:03:27.165
of Southland Tales

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:30.586
as amnesiac action star
Boxer Santaros.

00:03:33.964 --> 00:03:36.884
In the late 2000s, we saw
more of Dwayne's funny side,

00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:39.595
from putting himself in
the hands of Hannah Montana

00:03:40.262 --> 00:03:42.848
to squaring off against
funnyman Steve Carell

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:44.474
in Get Smart.

00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:48.145
His role as Agent 23
in the 2008 comedy

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.813
was the first time
he was credited

00:03:49.897 --> 00:03:52.524
as Dwayne Johnson
instead of The Rock.

00:03:53.275 --> 00:03:55.986
Though he still had
that classic Rock style.

00:04:00.741 --> 00:04:01.575
Thank you.

00:04:01.658 --> 00:04:04.620
The laughs kept on coming
when, in 2009,

00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.288
he hosted
Saturday Night Live

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:07.623
for the third time.

00:04:11.585 --> 00:04:12.586
And later that year,

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.588
he turned up
in Family Guy as himself

00:04:14.671 --> 00:04:16.965
to help censor
a raunchy love scene.

00:04:17.549 --> 00:04:18.425
Wow.

00:04:18.509 --> 00:04:20.677
Oh, and he played
the tooth fairy

00:04:20.761 --> 00:04:23.013
in 2010's Tooth Fairy.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.057
If this guy turned up
in your room at night,

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:26.767
you'd hand him
your entire gob,

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.060
no questions asked.

00:04:28.143 --> 00:04:29.478
And who could forget

00:04:29.561 --> 00:04:31.021
his turn alongside
Samuel L. Jackson

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:33.607
in 2010's The Other Guys

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.610
as the cocky and very
short-lived detective

00:04:36.693 --> 00:04:37.986
Christopher Danson.

00:04:41.865 --> 00:04:43.408
Luckily, Dwayne's
next character

00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:44.952
lasted a bit longer,

00:04:45.035 --> 00:04:47.955
the SS agent and bounty
hunter extraordinaire

00:04:48.038 --> 00:04:49.331
Lucas Hobbs.

00:04:49.414 --> 00:04:51.416
Above all else,
we don't ever,

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.836
ever let them
get in the cars.

00:04:53.919 --> 00:04:56.964
Chasing down the wrongfully
accused Dominic Toretto

00:04:57.047 --> 00:04:59.049
in 2011's Fast Five

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.385
was Johnson's ticket to
the blockbuster big leagues.

00:05:03.053 --> 00:05:05.931
The film took over $600
million at the box office

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.183
and established Hobbs
as a vital piece

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.394
of the Fast and Furious
universe.

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.899
Hobbs would return
four more times.

00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:17.985
In Fast &amp; Furious 6,
he worked alongside

00:05:18.068 --> 00:05:19.653
his one-time nemesis, Dom,

00:05:19.736 --> 00:05:22.322
to bring down Luke Evans'
dastardly Owen Shaw…

00:05:27.286 --> 00:05:28.871
in turn,
earning him the wrath

00:05:28.954 --> 00:05:30.873
of Jason Statham's
Deckard Shaw

00:05:30.956 --> 00:05:32.332
in Furious 7.

00:05:33.709 --> 00:05:35.794
By the time we reach
The Fate of the Furious

00:05:35.878 --> 00:05:37.129
in 2017,

00:05:37.212 --> 00:05:39.631
Hobbs was steering missiles
by hand.

00:05:39.715 --> 00:05:41.717
Is there anything
this guy can't do?

00:05:44.261 --> 00:05:46.388
Well, apart from get on
with Jason Statham,

00:05:46.471 --> 00:05:48.223
as proved
by their hilarious team-up

00:05:48.307 --> 00:05:50.475
in 2019's Hobbs and Shaw.

00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:52.394
Expect more banter
from these two

00:05:52.477 --> 00:05:54.354
as a sequel is in the works.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:58.275
While Dwayne spent
the last decade

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:01.195
destroying an entire car
festival's worth of motors,

00:06:01.278 --> 00:06:04.364
he built himself into
the ultimate leading man.

00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:07.159
In 2013, he went
from fast and furious

00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:09.161
to be vast and furious

00:06:09.244 --> 00:06:11.663
when he played a bodybuilder
turned kidnapper

00:06:11.747 --> 00:06:13.165
in Pain &amp; Gain.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.084
Then, in 2014,

00:06:16.168 --> 00:06:20.756
he played the man, the myth,
the legend, Hercules…

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:28.889
before returning
to modern day in 2015

00:06:28.972 --> 00:06:30.265
in San Andreas,

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:33.227
where he battled the largest
earthquake in history

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.021
as helicopter rescue pilot
Ray Gaines.

00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.064
Shit.

00:06:41.693 --> 00:06:44.321
Dwayne and San Andreas
director Brad Peyton

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.114
had so much fun
wrecking a city,

00:06:46.198 --> 00:06:47.866
they teamed up
to destroy another one

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.910
in 2018's Rampage.

00:06:53.121 --> 00:06:54.665
In 2015, Dwayne took on

00:06:54.748 --> 00:06:56.708
the biggest TV role
of his career

00:06:56.792 --> 00:06:58.585
as Spencer Strasmore,

00:06:58.669 --> 00:07:02.214
a retired NFL player turned
player-manager in Ballers.

00:07:02.297 --> 00:07:05.008
Think of it as
an NFL version of Entourage,

00:07:05.092 --> 00:07:07.261
with Johnson
on highly charismatic form

00:07:07.344 --> 00:07:09.179
over its five seasons.

00:07:09.263 --> 00:07:11.723
We got to hear
Dwayne's more tuneful side

00:07:11.807 --> 00:07:13.016
in 2016's Moana,

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:15.060
where he guided
the film's heroine

00:07:15.143 --> 00:07:17.479
as shapeshifting
demigod Maui.

00:07:19.231 --> 00:07:20.148
Sticking with the beach,

00:07:20.232 --> 00:07:23.360
but less family-friendly,
is 2017's Baywatch,

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.654
a raunchy take
on the 90s TV classic,

00:07:25.737 --> 00:07:28.991
where Dwayne played head
lifeguard Mitch Buchannon.

00:07:31.743 --> 00:07:34.037
In 2017's Jumanji:
Welcome to the Jungle,

00:07:34.121 --> 00:07:36.790
Dwayne continued to stretch
his comedy muscles

00:07:36.874 --> 00:07:38.458
and his actual muscles…

00:07:39.543 --> 00:07:41.962
as the smouldering
Dr Xander Bravestone,

00:07:42.045 --> 00:07:44.715
a video game action hero
possessed by the soul

00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:46.800
of a neurotic
high school student

00:07:47.384 --> 00:07:48.677
Do you have control of that

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.262
or does that just
happen naturally?

00:07:51.305 --> 00:07:52.723
It just happens naturally.

00:07:56.101 --> 00:07:58.937
A role so good, he repeated
the trick two years later

00:07:59.021 --> 00:08:00.731
in Jumanji: The Next Level,

00:08:00.814 --> 00:08:01.815
where, this time,

00:08:01.899 --> 00:08:04.568
he channelled the spirit
of Danny DeVito.

00:08:04.651 --> 00:08:06.737
Those are words
I never expected to say.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:08.697
Oh, my joints
feel like butter.

00:08:09.406 --> 00:08:11.283
Cementing
his action-hero credentials,

00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:13.619
Dwayne gave us
his own version of Die Hard

00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:15.704
in 2018's Skyscraper,

00:08:15.787 --> 00:08:17.748
where he played
a one-legged veteran

00:08:17.831 --> 00:08:20.375
saving his family from the
world's tallest building.

00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:23.462
Don't eat your dinner
during the jumping scene.

00:08:29.635 --> 00:08:31.470
If watching Dwayne Johnson's
Road to Netflix

00:08:31.553 --> 00:08:33.430
has left you wanting more
of his life story,

00:08:33.514 --> 00:08:36.141
you could check out
2021's Young Rock,

00:08:36.767 --> 00:08:38.435
a sitcom based
on his teenage years

00:08:38.519 --> 00:08:40.187
that jumps
between his school days

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.730
and early football career,

00:08:42.314 --> 00:08:45.192
and his life living
amongst wrestling legends.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.278
Which brings us
all the way to 2021

00:08:48.362 --> 00:08:51.490
and Dwayne's first
Netflix Original movie,

00:08:51.573 --> 00:08:52.658
Red Notice.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.869
If our trip through his
career taught us anything,

00:08:55.953 --> 00:08:57.621
it's that
he's just as comfortable

00:08:57.704 --> 00:08:59.289
wisecracking
as cracking skulls.

00:08:59.373 --> 00:09:03.919
And here he gets to do both
as FBI agent John Hartley.

00:09:04.002 --> 00:09:06.004
Tasked with bringing in
jewel thief Ryan Reynolds,

00:09:06.088 --> 00:09:07.381
he soon finds himself

00:09:07.464 --> 00:09:08.924
working with
his former nemesis

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:12.511
to bring down an even bigger
thief played by Gal Gadot.

00:09:12.594 --> 00:09:13.470
Arrest me.

00:09:13.554 --> 00:09:15.514
Make sure
you don't miss Red Notice,

00:09:15.597 --> 00:09:16.807
now streaming on Netflix,

00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:18.016
and to hear how more

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.394
of your favourite stars
took their road to Netflix,

00:09:20.477 --> 00:09:22.688
make sure you subscribe
to the channel.

